Z||000000||TRL46202||01-05-2000||04:30 PM||||Told them that I have an 87GT and they indicated that there records only go back 8yrs. So how do I know if my fiero had recall work done or not or does that matter at this point since there is no record of anything ever being done. Does this mean that I could get new stuff?? Also they told me that the only campaign that came up was for 1989. the number was 89V232000. Can someone explain........||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-05-2000||07:52 PM||||According to NHTSA... the governing body that governs recalls and the likes, a manufacturer is only obligated to perform recalls/store information about recalls 10 yrs.  Although I have heard various versions of this.  <P>To find out what the recalls are for your car, simply search the web with a good engine like metacrawler.  I have seen MANY pages with lists of the recalls for our cars.  Or head down to your local dealer.  Most of them will tell you if there are any outstanding recalls.<P>Good luck... William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000002||FieroMike||01-05-2000||08:10 PM||||That's B.S.  I called the same number and had my 84 2m4 recalled to the dealer to have a free inspection.  They re-routed the e-brake cable, and said that the recall had already been done for fire safety.  Tell them that... Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bruce||01-05-2000||08:39 PM||||I bought my 86GT in 1998 and called the dealer shortly after the purchase. They indicated that recall work needed to be done (e-brake cable, retrofit exhaust manifolds and heat shields, rear brake calipers). It was all done free and without hassle. I had mine done at Putnam Pontiac in Burlingame, Ca. Maybe you can call their service dept. and see if they have your VIN in the computer. The number is 650-342-4321.<BR>I'm fairly certain that there's no expiration date for GM recall work to be done- maybe you should *****  to the NTSB.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Clint||01-06-2000||08:26 AM||||I also was able to get recall info in 98 when i got my first car... In 99 however i wasn't able to get anything from PM cares. I belived they held all the fieros until the last car of the run hit 10 years. i.e. 88 was the last fiero.. 98 was the last year they supported.||||reg||1
